acy","best","best","mistake","miss","blunder","best","excellent","best","best","best","good","best","good","best","best","brilliant","best","best","good","excellent","good","good","best","good","best","best","good","best","best","best"],"moments":[{"ply":41,"name":"21.Bb3","cls":"miss","color":"w","headline":"21.Bb3 misses the chance 20…b5 gave: 21.Bxb5 would have punished it. White's winning chances go from 64% to 53%.","points":["Black answers 21…Nc8.","Better was 21.Bxb5 (+1.59), which takes the pawn on b5."],"better":"21.Bxb5 wins a pawn and trades off the attacked bishop instead of losing it to …bxc4. After 21…Bxb5 22.Rxd8 Bxe2 23.Rxe8 Rxe8 24.Rxe2 Nc8, White comes out a pawn up (+1.59)."},{"ply":43,"name":"22.Bc2","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"22.Bc2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked bishop to safety.","The next best move, 22.Rxd7, would drop White's winning chances from 53% to 33% (−1.94).","22.Bc2 gets the bishop out of the way of …axb3.","Black was threatening …axb3, winning a bishop for a pawn. The bishop steps away.","Black answers 22…Nc8.","Engine line: 22…Nc8 23.Ng4 Nd6 24.b3 Bc6 25.Bc1 (+0.27)."]},{"ply":56,"name":"28…Qg4","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"28…Qg4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Attacks the knight on f3, which is undefended.","The next best move, 28…Nh3+, would drop Black's winning chances from 52% to 21% (+3.65).","28…Qg4 wins a pawn, picking it up with 29…Qxg5.","Sets up a sequence and wins a pawn once the captures settle, picking it up with 29…Qxg5.","White answers 29.Nh2, attacking the queen.","After 29.Nh2 Qxg5 30.Nf3 Qg4 31.Nh2 Nh3+, Black comes out a pawn up (−0.28)."]},{"ply":74,"name":"37…hxg3","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"37…hxg3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the pawn on g3.","Pushes a pawn towards the White king, to pry open lines in front of it.","The next best move, 37…Bh6, would drop Black's winning chances from 82% to 69% (−2.14).","37…hxg3 stops Kh2.","White was threatening Kh2, winning a pawn, picking it up with 38.Qxh3. hxg3 takes care of it.","Takes the g3 pawn."]},{"ply":78,"name":"39…Bxc1","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"39…Bxc1! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the bishop on c1.","The next best move, 39…Nf2, would drop Black's winning chances from 65% to 40% (+1.15).","39…Bxc1 trades off the attacked bishop instead of losing it to Bxh6.","White was threatening Bxh6, winning a knight. The bishop takes something with it instead.","White answers 40.Rxc1, winning a knight.","After 40.Rxc1 Rh8 41.Qxh3+ Kg7 42.Nh4 Qxa2 43.Rb1, Black is two pawns down (−1.45)."]},{"ply":104,"name":"52…Ra1","cls":"miss","color":"b","headline":"52…Ra1 misses the chance 52.Rxc5 gave: 52…Rh1+ would have punished it. Black's winning chances go from 75% to 57%.","points":["White answers 53.h5, which pushes the passed pawn to h5.","Better was 52…Rh1+ (−2.97): the rook takes the half-open h-file."],"better":"52…Rh1+ takes the half-open h-file. After 53.Kg4 Rh2 54.Bd1 Nxe4 55.Rc6+ Kd7, Black comes out a pawn up (−2.97)."},{"ply":105,"name":"53.Ra5","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"53.Ra5 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 43% to 17%.","points":["Black answers 53…Rxa2, which takes the pawn on a2.","After Rxa2, Black wins 1 point of material within 2 moves.","Better was 53.h5 (−0.78), which pushes the passed pawn to h5."],"better":"53.h5 stops …Rxa2. After 53…Rc1 54.h6 Rh1+ 55.Kg3 Rxh6 56.Rc7, White is a pawn down (−0.78)."},{"ply":116,"name":"58…b2","cls":"brilliant","color":"b","headline":"58…b2!! A real sacrifice: Black gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Leaves the rook on e3 where it can be taken.","White can take, but after 59.Rxe3 b1=Q 60.Bg2 Qc1 the engine rates it −6.58.","Pushes the passed pawn to b2, close to promotion.","Moving away uncovers the rook on e3, which now hits the rook on a3.","58…b2 threatens …Rxa3, winning a rook.","It threatens …Rxa3, winning a rook, so White has to spend the next move on it."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"58…b2!! leaves the rook on e3 hanging. Taking it lets Black's pawn become a queen."},{"title":"What Black gives up","text":"58…b2 leaves the rook on e3 hanging to the rook on a3. That's a whole rook on offer."},{"title":"What it does instead","text":"It threatens …Rxa3, winning a rook."},{"title":"If White takes the rook","text":"59.Rxe3 is met by 59…b1=Q, threatening …Qxf1, winning a bishop. Then 60…Qc1 forks the rook and the pawn, and 61…Qd1+ gives check. Black ends up a piece and a pawn ahead: Black is winning (−6.38). This is White's best try."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 58…Nxe4, is clearly weaker (−4.94 against −6.58). White answers 59.Ra6+. Black would still be winning, but far less than after 58…b2."}]}],"opening":{"name":"Ruy Lopez: Morphy Defense, Steinitz Deferred","eco":"C79","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 11…Kh8: 22 moves in all, 11 by White and 11 by Black.","Theory runs out after 11…Kh8: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}